     The ppmmaapp__rreemmoovvee() function removes the range of addresses between _s_v_a and
     _e_v_a from the physical map _p_m_a_p.  If _e_v_a is less than _s_v_a, then the result
     is undefined.  It is assumed that both _s_v_a and _e_v_a are page-aligned ad‐
     dresses.

     The ppmmaapp__rreemmoovvee__aallll() removes the physical page _m from all physical maps
     in which it resides, and reflects back the modify bits to the appropriate
     pager.

     The ppmmaapp__rreemmoovvee__ppaaggeess() function removes all user pages from the physical
     map _p_m_a_p.  This function is called when a process exits to run down its
     address space more quickly than would be the case for calling
     ppmmaapp__rreemmoovvee().

